                                                "sense_id": "924f45f7-c5c3-392f-91de-af099ec1f386",
                                                "text": "The moistnesse which the roote of a tree suckes becomes a trunke, a leafe, and fruite: And the aire being but one, applied unto a trumpet, becommoth diverse in a thousand sorts of sounds."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
